# A Concept with no label.
#
# ConceptShape requires exactly one mng:label (minCount 1, maxCount 1). A
# concept that cannot be named is not a concept anything downstream can cite,
# which is why the cardinality is 1 rather than 0..1.
#
# The scope is present and well-formed on purpose, so the only thing wrong here
# is the missing label. An example broken in two places proves whichever check
# ran first.
@prefix mng: <https://w3id.org/cpcp/osi8/meaning#> .

<https://example.test/concept/nameless> a mng:Concept ;
  # INTENTIONALLY MISSING mng:label
  mng:scope <https://example.test/scope/finance> .
